    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai/surround\n\n### Description\n\nHaving\r\n```lua\r\nf(g(),\r\n  h())\r\n```\r\nmini.ai/surround can't match parentheses of `f()` because the searching algorithm search in the current line first.\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.7.2\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n2. Create a buffer with text\r\n```lua\r\nf(g(),\r\n  h())\r\n```\r\n3. Set cursor on the first `(`, type `va(` or `sh(`.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nSelect the parentheses of `f()`.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nParentheses of `g()` are selected.",
