        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "I also do love `cover_or_next`, but I expect to select `f()` when cursor on `f` or the first `(`, which targets.vim and builtin does. Only two positions could select `f()` with mini.ai is `,` and the last `)`. I think mini.ai should be an improved builtin, at least some option to make it behave more like builtin.",
